{"pattern_name": "Open Redirect Vulnerability", "functionality": "The code handles user registration by validating input, creating a registration request, and processing it through a service. Upon successful registration, it redirects the user to a specified URL or a default page.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code directly uses user-supplied input (`returnUrl`) in a redirect operation without validating whether the URL is safe or belongs to the application's domain. This allows attackers to craft malicious URLs that redirect users to external, potentially harmful sites.", "vulnerable_example": "public ActionResult Login(string returnUrl)
