{"pattern_name": "Missing Authorization in Database Operations", "functionality": "The code connects to a SQLite database, creates a table with specified columns and a primary key, and queries the database based on provided conditions. It returns the results of the query.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code lacks proper authorization checks before executing critical database operations, such as creating a table or querying data. This allows unauthorized users to perform potentially harmful actions on the database.", "vulnerable_example": "<?php
function createAndQueryTable($dbname, $table, $columns, $primaryKey, $conditions) {
    $db = new PDO("sqlite:$dbname");
    $db->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);
    $columnDefinitions = implode(", ", $columns);
    $sql = "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS $table ($columnDefinitions, PRIMARY KEY ($primaryKey))";
    $db->exec($sql); // Vulnerable line
